{#
    A page or a post of the blog itself, so it takes no panel, which is kept
    for what comes from other sites: faint lines above and below set it
    apart. The whole of it is the link, so it is one stop for the keyboard
    and its name says what it is before the title: "Related content:
    <title>". The title is no heading, so the outline of the page stays its own.
#}
<a class="group grid gap-1 border-y border-divider py-4 text-text no-underline" href="{{ url }}">
    <span class="text-base text-muted">{{ 'content.related_page.label'|trans }}<span class="sr-only">:</span></span>
    <span class="text-xl leading-snug font-semibold text-balance text-accent underline decoration-[0.06em] underline-offset-[0.18em] group-hover:text-accent-strong group-hover:decoration-[0.12em]">{{ title }}</span>
</a>
